## ================================ list ============================================
- list is collection of different datatypes as well as same data type
- we can store muitiple values in single variable
- it represent in between []
- it is a non primitive ,build-in-functions 
- it's is sequence collecton of values 
- list is mutable or changable or easy to modify
- it allowes duplicate values 
- it has indexing 



## ============COMMON METHODS ======================

| Method             | Purpose                     |
| ------------------ | --------------------------- |
| `append(x)`        | Add one element             |
| `extend(iterable)` | Add multiple elements       |
| `insert(i, x)`     | Insert at index             |
| `remove(x)`        | Remove first matching value |
| `pop([i])`         | Remove and return element   |
| `clear()`          | Remove all elements         |
| `index(x)`         | Find index of value         |
| `count(x)`         | Count occurrences           |
| `sort()`           | Sort the list               |
| `reverse()`        | Reverse the list            |
| `copy()`           | Create a shallow copy       |


## ================ use some built-in-functions============

- len(list)   it will show the what is the length of the list
- in          it is membership operator it checks the value  in the present list or not
- max         it will give highest value of your list 
- min         it will give least value of your list

